\begin_layout Section
Explainable AI
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
XAI deals with the problem of making AI solutions understandable for humans.
 As described in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "XAI_survey"
literal "true"

\end_inset

, a distinction is made between interpretability and explainability.
 Interpretability is defined as 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

the ability to explain or to present in understandable terms to humans
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 and is thus strongly related to the classical version of an explanation
 according to the cambridge dictionary, which defines an explanation as
 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

the details or reasons that someone gives to make something clear or easy
 to understand
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Flex URL
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/explanation
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset

 An explanation is a 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

collection of features of interpretable domain that have contributed for
 a given example to produce a decision
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Ein wichtiger Forschungspunkt stellt vor allem das nachträgliche Reasoning
 dar, wo ein bereits trainiertes Modell im Nachhinein erklärt werden soll.
 Wie gut
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Erklärbarkeit ist somit auch für Probleme möglich, die für Interpretierbarkeit
 zu komplex sind, wie beispielsweise die Bilderkennung.
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Image recognition is also not explainable to humans.
 To explain to another person what an object like a cat is, it is more helpful
 to show him a cat than to describe one.
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Layerwise Relevance Propagation
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Layerwise Relevance propagation 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "XAI_LRP_Frauenhofer"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 is a technique to determine the input features which were crucial for a
 neural network's output.
 In der Bilderkennung können so die wichtigsten Pixel erkennbar gemacht
 werden.
 This can help with debugging misbehaviour and also provides a good insight
 into machine vision.
 However, it can not provide additional trust.
 
\end_layout

